This repository is built on the starter scaffold for a transformer assignment, used
in INFO7375 (Semantic Intelligence in Large Language Models) at Northeastern
University and derived from CMU 11-667.

The scaffold itself derives from nanoGPT (Andrej Karpathy, MIT) and PyTorch; their
license texts are reproduced in copyright/.

Provided by the course, not written by me:

  src/lm/utils.py                device selection, parameter and disk-size estimates
  src/version.py
  src/tokenizer/english.py       trains the reference English tokenizer
  src/tokenizer/multilingual.py  English vs Thai token-count comparison
  src/tokenizer/visualize.py     prints a learned vocabulary
  src/pytest_utils/              Gradescope scoring plugin
  tests/test_env.py              environment checks
  tests/test_model.py            attention and forward-pass tests
  tests/test_train.py            sampler, schedule, loss and training tests
  tests/test_generate.py         temperature-sampling test
  configs/GPT-tiny.yaml          the baseline configuration
  scripts/                       formatting and submission helpers
  data/english-tokenizer.json, data/prefixes.jsonl, data/make_ppl_example_jsonl.py
  docs/STARTER_README.md         the original course README

Written by me:

  src/tokenizer/bpe.py           BPE merge, encode, decode; ASCII and Unicode variants
  src/lm/model.py                attention, feed-forward, decoder blocks, DecoderLM
  src/lm/train.py                samplers, cosine schedule, loss, training loop,
                                 plus checkpoint/resume and the int32 batch widening
  src/lm/generate.py             temperature sampling and batched generation
  src/lm/evaluate_perplexity.py
  src/lm/use_pythia.py
  configs/ (all but GPT-tiny.yaml)
  slurm/                         cluster bootstrap and all Slurm job scripts
  tests/test_tokenizer.py        the three counterexamples, and the offline fixture path
  results/, figures/, docs/      experiments, measurements and write-ups

The pre-tokenized training corpus is distributed by the course at
https://huggingface.co/datasets/yimingzhang/llms-hw2 and is not redistributed here.
